== Campaign ==

[[File:Lansarea candidaturii lui Victor Ponta la alegerile prezidentiale din 2014 - 20.09 (43) (15366505376).jpg|thumb|200px|[[Victor Ponta]] launching his candidature for the presidential election on [[Arena Națională|National Arena]], [[Bucharest]], 20 September]]
[[File:Lansarea candidaturii lui Victor Ponta la alegerile prezidentiale din 2014 - 20.09 (22) (15389531565).jpg|thumb|left|200px|Former [[Prime Minister of Moldova|Moldovan Prime Minister]] [[Iurie Leancă]] expressing his support for Victor Ponta at the launching of Ponta's campaign on the National Arena, Bucharest]]

[[Victor Ponta]] launched his campaign on his birthday, in a huge rally on the [[Arena Națională|National Arena]]. Over 70,000 people from across the country attended the rally.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-politic-18144200-victor-ponta-isi-lanseaza-sambata-candidatura-alegerile-prezidentiale-ziua-arena-nationala-sunt-asteptati-70-000-oameni.htm |title=Victor Ponta și-a lansat candidatura la prezidențiale, de ziua sa, în fața a zeci de mii de oameni, pe Arena Națională: Sunt Victor Viorel Ponta. Vă chem să fim împreună în bătălia pentru marea unire a românilor |work=HotNews.ro |author=I.R. |date=20 September 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> One of the stadium lawns was covered with four large panels inscribed with the slogan "Proud to be Romanians" and depicting Romanian folk motifs.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.realitatea.net/70-000-de-persoane-prezente-la-ziua-lui-victor-ponta-capitala-blocata_1529135.html |title=PONTA, lansare cu fast, pe Arena Națională: "Mi-e teamă să nu vă dezamăgesc!" |work=Realitatea.net |date=20 September 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> Many opposing political analysts, members of the opposition and even President [[Traian Băsescu]] have likened the event to the rallies in the communist period dedicated to [[Nicolae Ceaușescu]] or, more recently, those dedicated to [[Kim Jong-un]], the [[Supreme Leader of North Korea]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/politic/basescu-despre-lansarea-lui-ponta-omul-asta-si-a-pierdut-cumpatul-si-controlul-va-fi-vai-de-noi-cu-un-presedinte-ca-ponta-kim-jong-un-13313986 |title=Băsescu, despre lansarea lui Ponta: Omul ăsta și-a pierdut cumpătul și controlul. Va fi vai de noi cu un președinte ca Ponta, Kim Jong-Un |work=Mediafax.ro |author=Valentina Postelnicu |date=21 September 2014 |language=ro}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ziare.com/udrea/candidat-prezidentiale/ponta-comparat-cu-pigmeul-kim-jong-un-isi-construieste-cultul-maretului-conducator-1323090 |title=Ponta, comparat cu "pigmeul" Kim Jong Un: Își construiește cultul mărețului conducător |work=Ziare.com |author=Theodora Șopaltă |date=20 September 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> Likewise, he was criticized by PMP candidate Elena Udrea for the cost of organizing such an event which, she said, was around 2 million euros.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.evz.ro/elena-udrea-ponta-a-organizat-o-manifestare-ale-carei-costuri-intrec-orice-imaginatie-2-milioane-de-euro.html |title=Elena Udrea: Ponta a organizat o manifestare ale cărei costuri întrec orice imaginație: 2 milioane de euro |work=Evenimentul Zilei |date=20 September 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

[[Klaus Iohannis]] launched his campaign in front of the Government, in the presence of up to 30,000 people. The special guest of the event was the Secretary General of the EPP, [[Antonio López-Istúriz White]], who stated that "Victor Ponta cannot and should not become president of the European Romania".<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.gandul.info/politica/klaus-iohannis-s-a-lansat-in-cursa-pentru-cotroceni-din-fata-guvernului-nu-sunt-un-om-al-scandalului-si-al-spectacolului-13352676 |title=Klaus Iohannis s-a lansat în cursa pentru Cotroceni din fața Guvernului. "Nu sunt un om al scandalului și al spectacolului" |work=Gândul |author=Andi Manciu |date=27 September 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>  The vast majority of Romanians are [[Eastern Orthodox Christians]] like Ponta, while Iohannis is [[Protestant]]. Commenting on a poll, according to which 58.22% of the respondents said for them the religion of the President mattered, while 39.81% said they were indifferent to the issue, Ponta said he did not believe that a candidate for President "has a problem if he is Orthodox or is not of Romanian ethnicity".<ref name="EA">{{cite web |url=http://www.euractiv.com/sections/elections/ethnic-german-candidate-brings-suspense-romanias-presidential-race-307817 |title=Ethnic German candidate brings suspense to Romania's presidential race |work=EurActiv.com |date=18 August 2014}}</ref> Iohannis has reacted strongly to the statement by his rival, saying that bringing the issue of religion is a "painful attempt" to poison the campaign.<ref name="EA" /> Iohannis' slogan in the presidential campaign was "less talk, more things done", alluding to frequent television appearances of his rival, Victor Ponta.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.economist.com/news/europe/21615630-victor-ponta-running-against-four-centre-right-candidates-ponta-v-liberals-and-ladies |title=Romania's presidential election: Ponta vs the liberals and the ladies |newspaper=The Economist |date=6 September 2014}}</ref> In his presidential program are mentioned, among others: deepening of the strategic partnership with the United States, allocation of 2% of GDP for defense, 6% for health and 6% for education, restructuring of the management system of EU funds, development of the capital market, keeping the flat tax, return of VAT to 19%, etc.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-politic-18205623-principalele-puncte-din-programul-prezidential-lui-klaus-iohannis.htm |title=Principalele puncte din programul prezidențial al lui Klaus Iohannis |work=HotNews.ro |date=29 September 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> Iohannis proposes a liberal economy based on competitiveness and prosperity, encouragement of a highly developed agriculture, connection of Romania to the Western world through infrastructure or decentralization, as "vector of modernization". Likewise, for Klaus Iohannis, the European path of the [[Republic of Moldova]] is a national priority.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ziare.com/klaus-johannis/candidat-alegeri-prezidentiale-2014/klaus-iohannis-ce-promite-1325002 |title=Klaus Iohannis - Ce promite |work=Ziare.com |author=Camelia Badea |date=3 October 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

[[Elena Udrea]] launched her campaign for the presidency through an anti-governmental march attended by 10,000 people.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://adevarul.ro/news/politica/alegeri-prezidentiale-2014-elena-udrea-isi-lanseaza-astazi-candidatura-presedintie-printr-un-mars-1_5427bc710d133766a87d2d61/index.html |title=Alegeri prezidențiale 2014. Elena Udrea și-a lansat candidatura cu un marș: Nu sunt un om perfect, dar voi fi cel mai bun președinte |work=Adevărul |author=Mădălina Mihalache, Noémi Varga |date=28 September 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> She expressed her intention to dissolve the Parliament and form a new Government, in the eventuality that she would win the election.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.romanialibera.ro/politica/politica-alegeri-prezidentiale/elena-udrea--voi-dizolva-parlamentul-si-voi-propune-un-nou-premier--cu-un-nou-guvern-353821 |title=Elena Udrea: Voi dizolva Parlamentul și voi propune un nou premier, cu un nou Guvern |work=România Liberă |author=Paul Filimon |date=17 October 2014 |language=ro |access-date=27 October 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141025100100/http://www.romanialibera.ro/politica/politica-alegeri-prezidentiale/elena-udrea--voi-dizolva-parlamentul-si-voi-propune-un-nou-premier--cu-un-nou-guvern-353821 |archive-date=25 October 2014 |url-status=dead |df=dmy-all }}</ref> Udrea is supported by outgoing President [[Traian Băsescu]]<ref>{{cite web |url=https://jurnalul.ro/stiri/politica/basescu-cotroceni-elena-udrea-sustinere-679439.html |title=Băsescu, la Cotroceni, campanie pentru Udrea: Rămân consecvent în a susține candidatul PMP |work=Jurnalul Național |date=13 October 2014 |language=ro |access-date=27 October 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141027153359/http://jurnalul.ro/stiri/politica/basescu-cotroceni-elena-udrea-sustinere-679439.html |archive-date=27 October 2014 |url-status=live }}</ref> who intended to join the party Udrea leads at the end of his mandate in December.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-politic-18356177-elena-udrea-traian-basescu-inscrie-pmp-22-decembrie.htm |title=Elena Udrea: Traian Băsescu se va înscrie în PMP în 22 decembrie |work=HotNews.ro |author=I.C. |date=22 October 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

During the early days following the first round of the 2 November election, that saw the two main candidates from all opinion polls facing off in a 16 November runoff, several of the candidates that fell short of acceding into the second round have declared their support for one of the two remaining candidates. Prime Minister and [[Social Democratic Party (Romania)|PSD]] leader [[Victor Ponta]], who came first with 40.4% of the votes ahead of [[Sibiu]] mayor and [[Christian Liberal Alliance|ACL]] candidate [[Klaus Iohannis]] who earned a distant 30.3%, received the backing of the second runner-up, former premier and [[Senate of Romania|Senate]] president [[Călin Popescu-Tăriceanu]], from the [[Liberal Reformist Party (Romania)|Liberal Reformist Party]], who would also have been Ponta's proposal to replace him as Prime Minister, had Ponta won.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ziare.com/victor-ponta/calin-popescu-tariceanu/tariceanu-il-sustine-pe-ponta-si-refacerea-usl-batalia-nu-este-castigata-1331342 |title=Tăriceanu îl susține pe Ponta și refacerea USL: Bătălia nu este câștigată |work=Ziare.com |author=Alex Varzaru |date=4 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>
