Other candidates who also publicly declared their support for Ponta were: [[Dan Diaconescu]], from [[People's Party – Dan Diaconescu|PP-DD]], [[Corneliu Vadim Tudor]], from [[Greater Romania Party|PRM]] and independent candidate [[Teodor Meleșcanu]]. Despite [[Democratic Union of Hungarians in Romania|UDMR]]'s presence in the government led by Ponta, [[Hunor Kelemen]] expressed neutrality and recommended Hungarian electorate "vote according to their own beliefs". He said that UDMR can't support Victor Ponta in the second round because the Social Democrats have allied with PRM, an ultra-nationalist party, with which UDMR had several conflicts over time.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ziare.com/kelemen-hunor/candidat-alegeri-prezidentiale-2014/desi-este-la-guvernare-udmr-nu-l-sustine-pe-ponta-vezi-de-ce-1331774 |title=Deși este la guvernare, UDMR nu-l susține pe Ponta. Vezi de ce |work=Ziare.com |author=Georgeta Filip |date=6 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>  Internationally, Ponta received support from many current Prime Ministers across Europe, like the Moldovan premier [[Iurie Leancă]], Italian Prime Minister [[Matteo Renzi]], Serbian premier [[Aleksandar Vučić]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V4rbbV8WXGk|title=Aleksandar Vucic îl susține pe VICTOR PONTA|work=YouTube}}</ref> Slovak Prime Minister [[Robert Fico]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3R_6hWZ_jGE|title=Robert Fico îl susține pe VICTOR PONTA|work=YouTube}}</ref> Czech premier [[Bohuslav Sobotka]],<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vIWQwci-LZU|title = Bohuslav Sobotka îl susține pe VICTOR PONTA|website = [[YouTube]]}}</ref> Georgian premier [[Irakli Garibashvili]] and Albanian Prime Minister [[Edi Rama]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S1AhsgX-NXk|title=Edi Rama îl susține pe VICTOR PONTA|work=YouTube}}</ref> among others. Also, the [[Party of European Socialists]] expressed clear support for the candidature of Ponta to the Romanian presidency.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.agerpres.ro/english/2014/09/20/pm-victor-ponta-launched-his-candidacy-for-romania-s-presidency-20-10-43|title=PM Victor Ponta launched his candidacy for Romania's Presidency|access-date=16 November 2014}}</ref>
Others were [[Sigmar Gabriel]] (Germany, SPD),<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EyWvc3c9c14|title=Sigmar Gabriel îl susține pe VICTOR PONTA|work=YouTube}}</ref> [[Elio Di Rupo]] (Belgium, Parti Socialiste),<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v4fR5AmPJ6o|title=Elio Di Rupo îl susține pe VICTOR PONTA|work=YouTube}}</ref> [[Gianni Pittella]] (Italy)<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yKwJ_fNqSSI|title=Gianni Pittella îl susține pe VICTOR PONTA|work=YouTube}}</ref> and [[Martin Schulz]] (President of the [[European Parliament]]).<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BRv4BiBvMEM|title=Martin Schulz îl susține pe VICTOR PONTA|work=YouTube}}</ref>

Iohannis announced that he would not negotiate with other candidates, though he needed as much as 21% of the votes to recuperate and win. [[Elena Udrea]], from the [[People's Movement Party|PMP]]–[[Christian Democratic National Peasants' Party|PNȚCD]] Alliance, didn't avowedly express her support for Klaus Iohannis, but stated that the vote on 16 November should be anti-Ponta.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/politic/udrea-votul-in-turul-ii-trebuie-sa-fie-anti-ponta-dar-nu-sunt-adepta-raului-cel-mai-mic-13510029 |title=Udrea: Votul în turul II trebuie să fie anti-Ponta, dar nu sunt adepta "răului cel mai mic" |work=Mediafax.ro |author=Emma Toader |date=7 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> On the other hand, independents [[Monica Macovei]] and Mirel Mircea Amariței, as well as PPMT-backed Zsolt Szilágyi announced their support for Iohannis. Likewise, Iohannis enjoyed international support from the [[European People's Party]]<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.digi24.ro/Stiri/Digi24/Actualitate/Politica/PPE+il+va+sustine+pe+Klaus+Iohannis |title=PPE îl va susține pe Klaus Iohannis |work=Digi24 |date=11 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> and German Chancellor [[Angela Merkel]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://adevarul.ro/news/politica/alegeri-prezidentiale-2014-turul-doi-klaus-iohannis-vine-adevarul-live-ora-1200-pune-i-intrebari-candidatului-acl-presedintia-romaniei-1_54643da60d133766a8cfca84/index.html |title=Klaus Iohannis, la Adevărul Live: Mă susține Angela Merkel. Mi-a trimis și o scrisoare |work=Adevărul |author=Iulia Marin |date=13 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.siebenbuerger.de/zeitung/artikel/rumaenien/15002-deutsche-bundeskanzlerin-unterstuetzt.html |publisher=Siebenbürgische zeitung |title=Deutsche Bundeskanzlerin unterstützt Klaus Johannis |date=2014-11-14 |access-date=2014-11-17}}</ref>

Victor Ponta and key figures of his party accused Klaus Iohannis of wanting to separate [[Transylvania]] from the rest of Romania, because Iohannis won a large majority of the votes on 2 November in the intra-Carpathian region.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.foxnews.com/world/romanian-presidential-runoff-sets-pugnacious-pm-against-civilized-transylvanian-mayor/ |title=Romanian presidential runoff sets pugnacious PM against 'civilized' Transylvanian mayor |work=Fox News |date=13 November 2014}}</ref> Iohannis criticized these statements, describing them as "cretinisms". He also said that the idea of "breaking Transylvania" was "totally false, from another century and harmful", and came up because "people like the [[Greater Romania Party|PRM]] are coopted for some votes".<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/politic/iohannis-despre-acuzatiile-ca-ar-vrea-sa-rupa-ardealul-astea-nu-sunt-afirmatii-politice-ci-cretinisme-13506147 |title=Iohannis, despre acuzaţiile că ar vrea să rupă Ardealul: Astea nu sunt afirmații politice, ci cretinisme |work=Mediafax.ro |date=7 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> This topic was intensively discussed in local media. Many political commentators consider that dissimilar cultural heritage that each of the regions of Romania has is an exponent of the different vote expressed by [[Transylvania]], [[Banat]], [[Bukovina]], [[Crișana]] and [[Maramureș]], as opposed to [[Moldavia]], [[Wallachia]] and [[Dobruja]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://adevarul.ro/news/politica/cum-s-a-rupt-romania-tur-alegerilor-prezidentiale-2014-ar-sudul-estul-refuzapomenile-Tara-chiarmerita-timpuri-mai-bune-1_5465c1a80d133766a8d9ef04/index.html |title=Cum s-a rupt România după primul tur al prezidențialelor: "Ar fi bine dacă Sudul și Estul ar refuza pomenile. Țara asta chiar merită niște timpuri mai bune" |work=Adevărul |date=14 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

== Opinion polls ==
=== First round ===

The problem of the seriousness and confidence in the opinion polls in the political domain is extremely controversial in Romania. Many people, especially members and supporters of the opposition,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/politic/senator-pdl-psd-si-aliatii-sai-rasplatesc-din-bani-europeni-manipularile-sondajelor-de-opinie-12703304 |title=Senator PDL: PSD și aliații săi răsplătesc din bani europeni manipulările sondajelor de opinie |work=Mediafax.ro |author=Ela Giurgea |date=5 June 2014 |language=ro}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ziare.com/alegeri/alegeri-prezidentiale-2014/ponta-creste-de-la-o-saptamana-la-alta-in-sondajele-firmelor-apropiate-de-psd-1329872 |title=Ponta crește de la o săptămână la alta, în sondajele firmelor apropiate de PSD |work=Ziare.com |date=27 October 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> consider that the political affiliations of the directors of the main opinion polling firms have a significant impact in their results.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.dw.de/sondajele-sunt-falsificate-dar-nu-oricum/a-18001136 |title=Sondajele sunt falsificate, dar nu oricum |work=Deutsche Welle |author=Horațiu Pepine |date=17 October 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> For example, Sociopol is led by Mirel Palada, former spokesman for the government of [[Victor Ponta]],<ref name="sondaje">{{cite web |url=http://www.ziare.com/alegeri/alegeri-prezidentiale-2014/alegeri-prezidentiale-2014-cine-face-sondajele-de-opinie-1326022 |title=Alegeri prezidențiale 2014: Cine face sondajele de opinie |work=Ziare.com |date=6 October 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> while GSSC Avangarde is led by sociologist Marius Pieleanu, a confidant of the [[Conservative Party (Romania)|Conservative Party]].<ref name="sondaje" /> The honorary president of CSCI is Bogdan Teodorescu, one of the strategists of Victor Ponta's campaign during these presidential elections.<ref name="sondaje" /> The main shareholder of IRES is Vasile Dâncu, former PSD senator.<ref name="sondaje" /> But not only the ruling party has tangents with the opinion polls. CCSCC published the results of a fictional survey during the [[2014 European Parliament election in Romania|European Parliament election of 25 May 2014]], at liberal Horea Uioreanu's command, subsequently taken into custody for corruption.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/social/dna-uioreanu-a-primit-5-000-de-euro-mita-de-la-bene-care-a-platit-un-studiu-de-piata-fictiv-12668640 |title=DNA: Uioreanu a primit 5.000 de euro mită de la Bene, care a plătit un studiu de piață fictiv |work=Mediafax.ro |author=Andreea Unturică |date=31 May 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

Several opinion polls were conducted in the period preceding official announcement of the 14 candidates. Many of them showed [[Crin Antonescu]] instead of [[Klaus Iohannis]] or [[Cristian Diaconescu]] instead of [[Elena Udrea]]. In the polls also figured [[Mihai Răzvan Ungureanu]] and [[Cătălin Predoiu]], which withdrew their candidacies after the political events in the summer of 2014. The following table displays the main candidates (at least 1%) and evolution of their percentages.
{| class="wikitable"
|-align="center"
