===Confirmation of results===
On 21 November 2014, the [[Constitutional Court of Romania|Constitutional Court]] confirmed the results of the election and validated the election of [[Klaus Iohannis]] as [[President of Romania]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.ccr.ro/files/products/hotararea_621.pdf |title=Archived copy |access-date=2014-11-23 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150923201235/http://www.ccr.ro/files/products/hotararea_621.pdf |archive-date=2015-09-23 |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.ccr.ro/files/products/Hotararea_631.pdf |title=Archived copy |access-date=2014-11-23 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150923201232/http://www.ccr.ro/files/products/Hotararea_631.pdf |archive-date=2015-09-23 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

== Reactions ==

=== Protests ===
[[File:Vot și proteste la München 2 noiembrie 2014 Dan Mihai Pitea (4).JPG|thumb|200px|First round. Voters protesting in front of the General Consulate of [[Munich]], just minutes after the polls closed.]]
Several protests broke out in many cities abroad with large communities of Romanians. In [[Paris]], [[London]], [[Chișinău]], [[Munich]], [[Stuttgart]], [[Vienna]], [[Turin]] and other cities, Romanians expressed their dissatisfaction concerning the hindering of the voting process and closure before 9 p.m. of the polling stations.<ref name="diaspora">{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/politic/votul-in-diaspora-cozi-uriase-stampile-putine-proteste-porti-inchise-inainte-de-21-00-13486181 |title=Votul în diaspora: cozi uriașe, ștampile puține, proteste, porți închise înainte de 21:00 |work=Mediafax.ro |author=Cătălina Mihai |date=3 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> Protesters demanded the resignation of Foreign Minister [[Titus Corlățean]] and booed the Romanian Government led by PSD candidate [[Victor Ponta]]. In [[Paris]], the Romanian Embassy was assaulted by angry protesters. However, the situation defused after the intervention of special forces.<ref name="diaspora" />

[[File:Alegerile prezidențiale românești din 16 noiembrie 2014 la München (2).webm|thumb|left|Second round. A video depicting potential voters waiting and protesting in [[Munich]], approximately one hour before the polls closed on 16 November]]
Protests in solidarity with [[Romanian diaspora]] also took place in major Romanian cities.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-romania-election-protests-idUSKCN0IY29920141114 |title=Thousands protest in Romania ahead of presidential run-off vote |work=Reuters |author=Luiza Ilie |date=14 November 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.euronews.com/2014/11/15/romania-sees-protests-ahead-of-elections/ |title=Romania sees protests ahead of elections |work=Euronews |date=15 November 2014 |access-date=15 November 2014 |archive-date=19 November 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141119204514/http://www.euronews.com/2014/11/15/romania-sees-protests-ahead-of-elections |url-status=dead }}</ref> Organized on [[Facebook]], the protests attracted between 10,000 and 15,000 people in [[Cluj-Napoca]], 5,000 in [[Timișoara]], 4,000 in [[Bucharest]],<ref>{{cite web |url=http://adevarul.ro/news/bucuresti/bucurestenii-ies-nou-strada-s-au-plimbat-sediul-psd-4000-oameni-avem-arma-mai-puternica-decat-loc-democratia-1_5466fffd0d133766a8e247db/index.html |title=Bucureștenii ies din nou în stradă, după ce ieri s-au plimbat până la sediul PSD peste 4.000 de oameni. "Avem o armă mai puternică decât voi toți la un loc: democrația" |work=Adevărul |author=Cristina Răduță |date=15 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> 2,000 in [[Craiova]] and [[Sibiu]], 1,000 in [[Arad, Romania|Arad]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.gandul.info/stiri/zeci-de-mii-de-romani-au-iesit-in-strada-pentru-un-vot-corect-in-turul-doi-harta-protestelor-din-marile-orase-gandul-a-transmis-live-13550819 |title=Zeci de mii de români au ieșit în stradă pentru un vot corect în turul doi. HARTA PROTESTELOR din marile orașe. GÂNDUL A TRANSMIS LIVE |work=Gândul |author=Andrei Luca Popescu, Adriana Stanca |date=14 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> Many of the protesters were students, young people, intellectuals and people with higher education. They demanded fair elections and Victor Ponta's resignation as PM, whose image was associated with cartoon figures like [[Mickey Mouse]] and [[Pinocchio]]. [[Counter-protest]]s organized by sympathizers of PSD also took place in [[Galați]], [[Alba Iulia]], [[Bistrița]], [[Bacău]], [[Craiova]] and [[Brașov]], but were attended by fewer people.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-politic-18557239-livetext-mitinguri-solidaritate-romanii-din-strainatate-anuntate-mai-multe-orase-mari-din-tara.htm |title=Mitinguri masive în toată țara împotriva lui Ponta / În Cluj s-au adunat circa 10.000 de oameni / Câteva mii de protestatari din București au scandat la sediul PSD - Ieși afară, javră ordinară / Ponta, nu reziști nici cu mii de securiști! / Ponta, ce-a pățit procurorul Panait? |work=HotNews.ro |date=14 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

During a campaign visit at Millenium Hall, [[Baia Mare]], on 6 November, Victor Ponta was booed by hundreds of people protesting against his disinformation and manipulation uttered at his rival, [[Klaus Iohannis]], and condemning the statements in previous days of the premier and ministers [[Liviu Dragnea]], [[Titus Corlățean]] and Bogdan Stanoevici regarding the unfolding of voting process in diaspora.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.cotidianul.ro/victor-ponta-scos-cu-duba-ca-sa-fie-ferit-de-un-grup-de-protestatari-250701/ |title=Victor Ponta, scos cu duba ca să fie ferit de un grup de protestatari |work=Cotidianul.ro |author=Lucian Gheorghiu |date=6 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> In order to avoid any incidents, Prime Minister Victor Ponta was evacuated from the building by SPP agents and local policemen using a van-minibus.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ziare.com/victor-ponta/candidat-alegeri-prezidentiale-2014/ponta-huiduit-si-scos-cu-duba-din-multime-video-1331875 |title=Ponta, huiduit și scos cu duba din mulțime |work=Ziare.com |date=7 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

Victor Ponta accused rival party ACL of organizing the protests, but ACL denied these accusations. Moreover, leaders of ACL and candidate [[Klaus Iohannis]] saluted "the civic spirit of all Romanians who in recent days have protested (...) against candidate Victor Ponta's attempt to manipulate the Romanians vote".<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.gandul.info/politica/predoiu-ii-acuza-pe-ponta-si-corlatean-de-complot-acl-nu-a-fost-implicata-in-proteste-13517980 |title=Predoiu îi acuză pe Ponta și Corlățean de complot. "ACL nu a fost implicată în proteste" |work=Gândul |author=Andi Manciu |date=9 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

Poor organization of the second round in diaspora, but also violent dispersal of Romanian voters after the polls closed angered people in Romania that gathered in their tens of thousands in the largest protest against Ponta's government since the [[2013 Romanian protests against the Roșia Montană Project|demonstrations against the Roșia Montană Project in the autumn of 2013]].

=== Post-election ===
{{Quote box
|quote = Dear Romanians, all of you have been heroes today.
|author = [[Klaus Iohannis]], after the publication of first exit-polls<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.mediafax.ro/politic/iohannis-dragi-romani-ati-fost-niste-eroi-votul-a-decurs-fenomenal-o-prezenta-enorma-nu-mi-e-teama-va-multumesc-tuturor-13571563|title=Iohannis: Dragi români, aţi fost nişte eroi. Votul a decurs fenomenal, o prezenţă enormă. Nu mi-e teamă. Vă mulţumesc tuturor|website=Mediafax.ro}}</ref>
|align = right}}
The final result was widely seen as a surprise, as all polls before the second round showed Ponta as a clear favorite over Iohannis.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.ft.com/intl/cms/s/0/4ddc6ae6-6ddb-11e4-8f96-00144feabdc0.html#axzz3JKD3cDYw|title=Iohannis wins Romanian election - FT.com|work=Financial Times|date=17 November 2014}}</ref><ref name=NYT>{{Cite news|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/17/world/europe/favorite-concedes-presidency-in-romania.html|title=Favorite Concedes Presidency in Romania (Published 2014)|first=Kit|last=Gillet|newspaper=The New York Times|date=November 17, 2014}}</ref><ref name=telegraph>{{cite web|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/11234915/Romanian-presidential-election-victory-for-centre-right-candidate-Klaus-Iohannis.html|title=Romanian presidential election victory for centre-right candidate Klaus Iohannis|date=16 November 2014|work=Telegraph.co.uk}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://news.yahoo.com/romanian-pm-concedes-surprise-defeat-presidential-vote-231818750.html|title=Surprise presidential victory for Romania's Iohannis|date=17 November 2014|work=Yahoo News}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.novinite.com/articles/164797/Klaus+Iohannis+Wins+Romania+Presidential+Vote|title=Klaus Iohannis Wins Romania Presidential Vote - Novinite.com - Sofia News Agency|website=www.novinite.com}}</ref> Ponta did not give a speech at 9 p.m. when the polling ended, and a few hours later he conceded defeat, declaring that "the people are always right" and congratulating Klaus Iohannis over the phone.<ref name=NYT/><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/europe/victor-ponta-loses-to-klaus-iohannis-in-romanias-presidential-runoff-9864057.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220501/https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/europe/victor-ponta-loses-to-klaus-iohannis-in-romanias-presidential-runoff-9864057.html |archive-date=2022-05-01 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live|title=Victor Ponta loses to Klaus Iohannis in Romania's presidential run-off|work=The Independent|date=16 November 2014}}{{cbignore}}</ref> Cristian Ghinea of the Romanian Center for European Policies considered that "Iohannis did a poor job in the two debates, but Ponta mobilized the people against himself (...) He ran a dirty campaign which blew up in his face",<ref name=NYT/> while [[Sergiu Mișcoiu|Sergiu Miscoiu]], an analyst, thought that "a major mistake was ostracizing the diaspora".<ref name=telegraph/> Ponta ruled out quitting as prime minister until the parliamentary elections in 2016.<ref name=telegraph/> Only about 10% of diaspora ended up voting for Ponta.<ref name=real>{{Cite web|url=https://www.realitatea.net/stiri/ultimele-stiri/klaus-iohannis-castigator-klaus-iohannis-noul-presedinte-romania_5dcc91df406af85273ce309a|title=Klaus Iohannis, castigator: Ne-am luat tara inapoi. Klaus Iohannis e noul presedinte al Romaniei|date=November 17, 2014|website=Realitatea.NET}}</ref>

Upon closing of the polls in Romania, Klaus Iohannis thanked voters for the high turnout and asked the Government to extend the voting period in diaspora to allow everyone in line to vote. Later in the evening, when the victory became clear, he went to [[University Square, Bucharest|University Square]], [[Bucharest]], where up to 20,000 people were celebrating, and declared that "we took our country back".<ref name=real/><ref>{{cite web|url=http://stirileprotv.ro/stiri/alegeri-prezidentiale-2014/primele-declaratii-ale-lui-klaus-iohannis-dupa-exit-poll-uri-dragi-romani-ati-fost-niste-eroi.html|title=Klaus Iohannis a fost in Piata Universitatii si le-a multumit oamenilor: "Am castigat! Ne-am luat tara inapoi"|work=stirileprotv.ro}}</ref> On Monday morning Iohannis declared that he will be a free president that will represent all Romanians.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mediafax.ro/politic/iohannis-prima-declaratie-oficiala-dragi-romani-va-multumesc-voi-fi-un-presedinte-liber-va-voi-reprezenta-pe-voi-solicitarile-lui-iohannis-13576745|title=Iohannis, prima declaraţie oficială: Dragi români, vă mulţumesc. Voi fi un preşedinte liber, vă voi reprezenta pe voi. SOLICITĂRILE lui Iohannis|work=Mediafax.ro}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://evz.ro/klaus-iohannis-dragi-romani-va-multumesc.html|title=Klaus Iohannis: Dragi români, vă mulțumesc|last=Otilia|first=Luca|date=November 17, 2014|website=Evenimentul Zilei}}</ref>

Following the elections, a wave of resignations occurred in the PSD.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-politic-18586938-prima-demisie-din-psd-dupa-alegeri-gabriel-zetea-presedintele-psd-maramures-plecat-din-partid.htm | title=Prima demisie dupa alegeri: Gabriel Zetea, presedintele PSD Maramures, a demisionat | date=17 November 2014 | access-date=20 November 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.evz.ro/demisii-in-psd-constanta-dupa-rezultatul-dezastruos-al-alegerilor-prezidentiale-radu-mazare-se-mai-gandeste.html | title=Demisii în PSD Constanţa după rezultatul "dezastruos" al alegerilor prezidenţiale. Radu Mazăre se mai gândeşte | access-date=20 November 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.realitatea.net/demisii-pe-banda-in-psd-dupa-votul-din-diaspora_1573896.html | title=DEMISII pe bandă în PSD, după votul din Diaspora | date=19 November 2014 | access-date=20 November 2014}}</ref> Foreign Minister Teodor Meleșcanu also resigned following the diaspora voting fiasco, thus setting a record for the shortest term as minister in Romania's post-Communist history, having served for only eight days.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://stirileprotv.ro/stiri/politic/ministrul-de-externe-teodor-melescanu-sustine-o-conferinta-de-presa-live-ora-10-30.html | title=Ministrul Afacerilor Externe, Teodor Melescanu, si-a dat marti demisia si a stabilit un record national: a fost ministrul plin cu cel mai scurt mandat din istoria post decembrista, adica 8 zile | access-date=20 November 2014}}</ref> PSD senator Mircea Geoană, who ran unsuccessfully against Traian Băsescu in the [[2009 Romanian presidential election|2009 presidential elections]], characterized the result as a "dramatic moment for the Romanian Left" and warned that the PSD needs to "reinvent itself".<ref>{{cite web | url=http://vreaupresedinte.gandul.info/news/avertismentul-lui-geoana-situatia-psd-mai-grava-decat-in-2004-votul-negativ-a-fost-de-o-intensitate-fara-precedent-13580966 | title=Avertismentul lui Geoană: Situaţia PSD, mai gravă decât în 2004; votul negativ a fost de o intensitate fără precedent | access-date=20 November 2014}}</ref> President-elect Iohannis stated that he want to topple the government.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.repubblica.it/esteri/2014/12/03/news/iohannis_sfida_putin_la_mia_romania_vuole_un_europa_forte-102003307/?ref=search |title=Iohannis: "La mia Romania vuole un'Europa forte" |work=La Repubblica |author=Andrea Tarquini |language=it |date=3 December 2014}}</ref> In this regard, PNL leaders intend to file a [[motion of censure]] at the beginning of 2015.

==== International ====
* {{flagicon|United States}} [[U.S. Government]] congratulated President-elect Klaus Iohannis for his appointment, but also "Romanians, who went to the polls in large numbers, both in country and abroad, in an exemplary demonstration of civic participation".<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/politic/guvernul-sua-il-felicita-pe-klaus-iohannis-pentru-alegerea-ca-presedinte-13611967 |title=Guvernul SUA îl felicită pe Klaus Iohannis pentru alegerea ca președinte |work=Mediafax.ro |date=21 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>
* {{flagicon|EU}} [[Joseph Daul]], President of the [[European People's Party]], congratulated Klaus Johannis for the victory in the presidential election, specifying it is "an excellent news" for Romania and the [[European Union]]. He stated that Iohannis "will maintain Romania on the democratic way and will lead it in the interest of the Romanian people". On the other hand, Daul expressed disappointment with the "bad conditions" of voting in diaspora.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/politic/joseph-daul-victoria-lui-klaus-iohannis-o-veste-excelenta-pentru-romania-si-pentru-ue-13578519 |title=Joseph Daul: Victoria lui Klaus Iohannis - o veste excelentă pentru România și pentru UE |work=Mediafax.ro |author=Cătălina Mihai |date=17 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> Likewise, the [[European Commission President]] [[Jean-Claude Juncker]] has sent to President-elect of Romania, Klaus Iohannis, a congratulatory letter expressing eagerness to work with the new head of state and government of the country for implementation of the EU agenda, focusing on jobs, investment, competitiveness and growth.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-esential-18627514-presedintele-felicita-iohannis-abia-astept-lucrez-dumneavoastra-guvernul-implementarea-agendei-strategice-pentru.htm |title=Președintele CE îl felicită pe Iohannis: De-abia aștept să lucrez cu dumneavoastră și cu Guvernul la implementarea agendei strategice pentru UE |work=HotNews.ro |author=Claudiu Zamfir |date=21 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>
* {{flagicon|UK}} [[British PM]] [[David Cameron]] also sent Iohannis a congratulatory letter. In reply, Iohannis thanked for it and assured Cameron of strengthening the bilateral relations between the two countries.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.digi24.ro/Stiri/Digi24/Actualitate/Politica/Klaus+Iohannis+il+asigura+pe+Cameron+de+intregul+sau+sprijin+pen |title=Klaus Iohannis îl asigură pe David Cameron de întregul său sprijin pentru întărirea relațiilor bilaterale |work=Digi24 |date=4 December 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>
* {{flagicon|Germany}} [[German President]] [[Joachim Gauck]] congratulated Klaus Iohannis for victory in the presidential election and assured that Germany would continue to support Romania on track of important reforms, particularly in terms of strengthening the rule of law.<ref name="felicitari">{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/externe/presedintele-si-cancelarul-germaniei-l-au-felicitat-pe-iohannis-gauck-vom-sprijini-romania-in-consolidarea-statului-de-drept-merkel-vom-aprofunda-relatiile-bilaterale-13587083 |title=Președintele și cancelarul Germaniei l-au felicitat pe Iohannis. Gauck: Vom sprijini România în consolidarea statului de drept. Merkel: Vom aprofunda relațiile bilaterale |work=Mediafax.ro |author=Cătălina Mihai |date=18 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> Chancellor [[Angela Merkel]] also congratulated Iohannis, stressing that together will deepen bilateral relations.<ref name="felicitari" />
* {{flagicon|France}} "I am pleased to address my sincere congratulations and my wishes of success in fulfilling your high mission", said [[French President]] [[François Hollande]] in a letter sent to Klaus Iohannis. The letter also shows: "Together with you, I want to build a more prosperous, fairer and stronger, able Europe, at times when faces various crises in its neighborhood, to spread its characteristic values, namely democracy and respect for the rule of law".<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.digi24.ro/Stiri/Digi24/Special/COTROCENI+2014/Francois+Hollande+l-a+felicitat+pe+Klaus+Iohannis+pentru+castiga |title=F. Hollande l-a felicitat pe K. Iohannis: Îmi face plăcere să vă invit la Paris, în funcție de agenda dumneavoastră |work=Digi24 |date=19 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>
* {{flagicon|Russia}} Spokesman for the Russian Foreign Ministry, Alexander Lukashevich, expressed Moscow's position on the presidential election, expressing the hope that, after the election of Klaus Iohannis, the two countries will register a "major change" in their relations after the break caused by "Bucharest's criticism over Moscow's policies" concerning the [[Russo-Ukrainian war]], but also other international issues.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.gandul.info/international/primul-mesaj-al-rusiei-dupa-castigarea-alegerilor-de-catre-klaus-iohannis-13606588 |title=Primul mesaj al Rusiei după câștigarea alegerilor de către Klaus Iohannis |work=Gândul |author=Mihaela Stoica |date=20 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>
* {{flagicon|Hungary}} [[President of Hungary]], [[János Áder]], conveyed his congratulations to Iohannis for victory in the presidential election. In a letter sent to Iohannis, János Áder requested a meeting between the two leaders to discuss issues of mutual interest and to analyze the directions of bilateral cooperation.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/externe/presedintele-ungariei-janos-ader-l-a-felicitat-pe-klaus-iohannis-13591277 |title=Președintele Ungariei, Janos Ader, l-a felicitat pe Klaus Iohannis |work=Mediafax.ro |author=Mihai Drăghici |date=18 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

