== Controversies ==
The candidate of Christian Liberal Alliance, [[Klaus Iohannis]], publicly asked Prime Minister [[Victor Ponta]] for the cancellation of Ordinance 45 of 2014, that amends the legislation on presidential elections,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.b1.ro/stiri/politica/klaus-iohannis-ii-cere-premierului-victor-ponta-amanarea-alegerilor-preziden-iale-din-toamna-88954.html |title=Klaus Iohannis îi cere premierului Victor Ponta amânarea alegerilor prezidențiale din toamnă |work=B1.ro |date=11 August 2014 |language=ro |access-date=25 September 2014 |archive-date=10 October 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141010002707/http://www.b1.ro/stiri/politica/klaus-iohannis-ii-cere-premierului-victor-ponta-amanarea-alegerilor-preziden-iale-din-toamna-88954.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> affirming that these changes might lead to [[electoral fraud]] by favoring multiple voting.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.digi24.ro/Stiri/Digi24/Actualitate/Politica/Klaus+Iohannis+cere+amanarea+alegerilor+prezidentiale |title=K. Iohannis cere anularea HG care stabilește data prezidențialelor: Nu e normal ca Guvernul să creeze un avantaj pentru V. Ponta |work=Digi24 |date=11 August 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> In this regard, PNL brought to trial the Government.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.romanialibera.ro/politica/partide/iohannis--pnl-da-in-judecata-guvernul-pentru-ordonanta-care-modifica-legea-electorala-345337 |title=Iohannis: PNL dă în judecată Guvernul pentru ordonanța care modifică Legea electorală |work=România Liberă |author=Avram Eliza |date=5 August 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> [[Cristian Diaconescu]], then the presidential candidate of [[People's Movement Party|PMP]], notified by letter the Venice Commission about this issue.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.b1.ro/stiri/politica/pmp-sesizeaza-comisia-de-la-vene-ia-cu-privire-la-legea-pentru-alegerea-pre-edintelui-85897.html |title=PMP sesizează Comisia de la Veneția cu privire la legea pentru alegerea președintelui |work=B1.ro |date=28 June 2014 |language=ro |access-date=25 September 2014 |archive-date=10 October 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141010004243/http://www.b1.ro/stiri/politica/pmp-sesizeaza-comisia-de-la-vene-ia-cu-privire-la-legea-pentru-alegerea-pre-edintelui-85897.html |url-status=dead }}</ref>

In September, the candidacies of [[Victor Ponta]] and [[Monica Macovei]] were contested at the [[Constitutional Court of Romania|Constitutional Court]], but the complaints were rejected by the court.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.realitatea.net/candidaturile-lui-ponta-si-macovei-contestate-ccr-anunta-astazi-decizia_1531242.html |title=Candidaturile lui Ponta și Macovei, CONTESTATE. CCR le-a RESPINS |work=Realitatea.net |date=23 September 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> On the other hand, the National Integrity Agency (ANI) announced in April 2013 that it believed [[Klaus Iohannis]] was in a 'state of incompatibility',<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ziare.com/klaus-johannis/primar-sibiu/dosarul-de-incompatibilitate-al-lui-klaus-iohannis-inalta-curte-a-stabilit-termenul-de-judecata-surse-1323731 |title=Dosarul de incompatibilitate al lui Klaus Iohannis: Înalta Curte a stabilit termenul de judecată |work=Ziare.com |date=23 September 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> because he has been the representative of [[Sibiu]] in the General Meeting of Shareholders of SC Apă Canal SA Sibiu (since 5 August 2010) and of SC Piețe SA (since 30 April 2009), which contravenes legal provisions governing conflicts of interest.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://stirileprotv.ro/stiri/actualitate/iccj-a-stabilit-primul-termen-pentru-joi-in-dosarul-de-incompatibiliate-al-lui-klaus-iohannis.html |title=Curtea Supremă a amânat procesul lui Iohannis cu ANI pentru 30 septembrie |work=Știrile Pro TV |date=25 September 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> Iohannis repeatedly said that ANI's claims to that effect were mistaken.{{citation needed|date=November 2014}}

Iohannis was also attacked by his rivals, especially Victor Ponta, on the topic of the provenance of his six estates. Many supporters of PSD and TV stations with some sympathies for this party stated that Iohannis bought these houses illicitly,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.realitatea.net/romania-tv-a-inceput-execu-ia-lui-iohannis_1458583.html |title=România TV a început "EXECUȚIA" lui Iohannis |work=Realitatea.net |date=10 June 2014 |language=ro |access-date=21 October 2014 |archive-date=21 October 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141021152010/http://www.realitatea.net/romania-tv-a-inceput-execu-ia-lui-iohannis_1458583.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> statements which were later refuted by Iohannis. He explained that he has bought the six houses by "honest work" and that the money to purchase them originated either from his own sources – salaries, tutoring, rents - or from money received from his parents and parents-in-law or from loans from friends.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.gandul.info/politica/iohannis-explica-sursa-banilor-pentru-cele-sase-case-parinti-socri-meditatii-salariu-chirii-imprumuturi-13417856 |title=Iohannis explică sursa banilor pentru cele șase case: părinți, socri, meditații, salariu, chirii, împrumuturi |work=Gândul |author=Cristian Andrei |date=20 October 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

=== Diaspora voting ===
[[File:Alegerile prezidențiale românești din 16 noiembrie 2014 la München (1).webm|thumb|Second round. The waiting line in [[Munich]], Germany, before 8 a.m.|left|421x421px]]

The first round of voting was marked by a scandal concerning the small number of polling stations in countries with large communities of Romanian citizens. 294 polling stations were organized in 95 states,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/politic/alegeri-prezidentiale-2014-in-strainatate-sunt-294-de-sectii-primii-voteaza-cei-din-noua-zeelanda-13482717 |title=ALEGERI PREZIDENȚIALE 2014: În străinătate sunt 294 de secții. Primii votează cei din Noua Zeelandă |work=Mediafax.ro |author=Cătălina Mihai |date=31 October 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> given that over 3 million Romanians with voting right are living and working abroad. In cities like [[London]], [[Paris]], [[Madrid]], [[Vienna]], [[Munich]], [[Stuttgart]], [[Turin]], [[Rome]] or [[Chișinău]] huge queues of voters were reported at embassies or other polling stations.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://english.hotnews.ro/stiri-top_news-18444455-romanian-voters-abroad-humiliated-government-organisers-forced-them-wait-for-hours-long-queues-european-cities-presidential-poll.htm |title=Romanian voters abroad humiliated: government organisers forced them to wait for hours in long queues in European cities in presidential poll |work=HotNews.ro |author=V.O. |date=3 November 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.romania-insider.com/chaos-at-romanias-voting-polls-abroad-long-queues-protests/134937/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141107070609/http://www.romania-insider.com/chaos-at-romanias-voting-polls-abroad-long-queues-protests/134937/ |url-status=dead |archive-date=7 November 2014 |title=Chaos at Romania's voting polls abroad: long queues, protests |work=Romania-Insider.com |date=3 November 2014 }}</ref> They claim they were prevented from exercising their right to vote, inasmuch as thousands of voters were locked outside the embassies and could not vote until the polls closed.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/news/london/thousands-of-romanians-locked-outside-london-embassy-denied-their-right-to-vote-9834568.html |title=Hundreds of Romanians locked outside London Embassy 'denied their right to vote' |work=London Evening Standard |author=Anna Dubuis |date=3 November 2014}}</ref> Presidential candidates [[Klaus Iohannis]], [[Elena Udrea]] and [[Monica Macovei]] urged the prolongation of the voting process in these countries.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://ro.stiri.yahoo.com/monica-macovei-cere-prelungirea-programului-%C3%AEn-sec%C5%A3iile-votare-164818263.html |title=Alegeri prezidențiale 2014. Monica Macovei cere prelungirea programului în secțiile de votare din străinătate și a depus mai multe contestații |work=Yahoo! News |date=2 November 2014 |language=ro |access-date=3 November 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141103221803/https://ro.stiri.yahoo.com/monica-macovei-cere-prelungirea-programului-%C3%AEn-sec%C5%A3iile-votare-164818263.html |archive-date=3 November 2014 |url-status=dead |df=dmy-all }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.romanialibera.ro/politica/politica-alegeri-prezidentiale/iohannis-a-denuntat-proasta-organizare-a-alegerilor-in-tara-si-diaspora--a-cerut-bec-prelungirea-votarii-355748 |title=Klaus Iohannis a denunțat PROASTA ORGANIZARE a alegerilor în țară și diaspora. A cerut BEC prelungirea votării |work=România Liberă |author=Paul Filimon |date=2 November 2014 |language=ro |access-date=3 November 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141130015939/http://www.romanialibera.ro/politica/politica-alegeri-prezidentiale/iohannis-a-denuntat-proasta-organizare-a-alegerilor-in-tara-si-diaspora--a-cerut-bec-prelungirea-votarii-355748 |archive-date=30 November 2014 |url-status=dead |df=dmy-all }}</ref> Moreover, the Presidential Administration demanded in a release the immediate resignation of Foreign Minister [[Titus Corlățean]] and Minister Delegate for Romanians Abroad Bogdan Stanoevici for poor organization of election in diaspora.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.realitatea.net/traian-basescu-cere-demisia-mini-trilor-corla-ean-i-stanoevici_1561027.html |title=TRAIAN BĂSESCU cere DEMISIA miniștrilor CORLĂȚEAN și STANOEVICI |work=Realitatea.net |date=2 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> Likewise, independent candidate [[Gheorghe Funar]] submitted an application to the President of BEC, demanding the cancellation of the first round of voting and its resumption because he considers that the equality of citizens before the law was not ensured, and the right to vote of Romanians abroad was seriously violated.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.agerpres.ro/politica/2014/11/02/funar-cere-anularea-si-reluarea-primului-tur-al-alegerilor-prezidentiale-20-52-19 |title=Funar cere anularea și reluarea primului tur al alegerilor prezidențiale |work=Agerpres |date=2 November 2014 |language=ro |access-date=3 November 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141103153752/http://www.agerpres.ro/politica/2014/11/02/funar-cere-anularea-si-reluarea-primului-tur-al-alegerilor-prezidentiale-20-52-19 |archive-date=3 November 2014 |url-status=dead |df=dmy-all }}</ref> These problems determined [[Gunther Krichbaum]], the chairman of the Commission for European Affairs in the Bundestag to declare that the issue at stake does not concern "possible difficulties in the organisation of elections, but a wilful hindrance of the free expression of the votes", based on the current leftist government's knowledge of the fact that "Romanians living abroad have the tendency to vote with the parties and candidates of the centre-right".<ref name="actmedia.eu/daily/the-chairman-of-the-commission-for-european-affairs-in-bundestag-writes-to-juncker-the-sections-outside-romania-received-indications-from-bucharest-to-hinder-the-vote/54970_2014-11-29">{{Citation | url=http://actmedia.eu/daily/the-chairman-of-the-commission-for-european-affairs-in-bundestag-writes-to-juncker-the-sections-outside-romania-received-indications-from-bucharest-to-hinder-the-vote/54970| title=The chairman of the Commission for European Affairs in Bundestag writes to Juncker: the sections outside Romania received indications from Bucharest to hinder the vote| newspaper=Actmedia.eu/daily/the-chairman-of-the-commission-for-european-affairs-in-bundestag-writes-to-juncker-the-sections-outside-romania-received-indications-from-bucharest-to-hinder-the-vote/54970| access-date=29 November 2014}}</ref>  Irregularities were also reported in the country's major university centers, where students were forced to form queues of hundreds of people or were redirected to other polling stations, as the standardized affidavit forms had run out.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.gandul.info/reportaj/apelul-studentilor-din-regie-care-nu-au-putut-vota-vrem-sa-votam-asta-e-democratia-lui-ponta-13486137 |title=Apelul studenților din Regie care nu au putut vota: "Vrem să votăm! Asta e democrația lui Ponta?" |work=Gândul |author=Andreea Ofițeru |date=3 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

Angry voters staged spontaneous protests in front of the polling stations in [[Paris]], [[Vienna]], [[London]], [[Madrid]], [[New York City]], [[Strasbourg]] and many other locations, chanting slogans like "Down with Ponta!", "Plagiarized vote" or "We want to vote".<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.gandul.info/stiri/alegeri-prezidentiale-2014-mii-de-romani-au-protestat-la-londra-scandand-jos-ponta-vot-plagiat-si-vrem-sa-votam-13485988 |title=ALEGERI PREZIDENȚIALE 2014. Mii de români au protestat la Londra, scandând "Jos Ponta!", "Vot plagiat" și "Vrem să votăm" |work=Gândul |author=Clarice Dinu |date=2 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> In [[Paris]], [[Vienna]], [[London]] and [[Turin]] protests escalated in storming embassies and consulates. Spirits were calmed only after the intervention of law enforcement.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ziare.com/alegeri/alegeri-prezidentiale-2014/romanii-au-fortat-votul-dupa-inchiderea-urnelor-la-paris-viena-si-londra-jandarmii-au-intervenit-1331006 |title=Românii au forțat votul după închiderea urnelor la Paris, Viena și Londra - jandarmii au intervenit |work=Ziare.com |author=Irina Olteanu, Cristian Soitu |date=3 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

Under pressure from street protests that followed the first round, Titus Corlățean resigned on 10 November.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-romania-election-minister/romanian-foreign-minister-resigns-in-election-row-idUSKCN0IU0Y620141110 |title=Romanian foreign minister resigns in election row |work=[[Reuters]] |author=Radu-Sorin Marinaș |date=10 November 2014}}</ref> Prime Minister Victor Ponta proposed former presidential candidate [[Teodor Meleșcanu]] to occupy this position. The same day, Meleșcanu took the oath in front of President Traian Băsescu at the [[Cotroceni Palace]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/politic/teodor-melescanu-a-depus-juramantul-de-investitura-in-functia-de-ministru-de-externe-basescu-demisia-lui-corlatean-a-intervenit-prea-tarziu-il-numesc-pe-melescanu-datorita-urgentei-13523461 |title=Teodor Meleșcanu a depus jurământul de învestitură în funcția de ministru de Externe. Băsescu: Demisia lui Corlățean a intervenit prea târziu. Îl numesc pe Meleșcanu "datorită urgenței" |work=Mediafax.ro |date=10 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

Despite measures taken by new Minister of Foreign Affairs, the scandal in the first round repeated in the second one, but in higher proportions. Kilometer-long queues were reported in several European cities, including [[Paris]], [[Strasbourg]], [[London]], [[Dublin]], [[Brussels]], [[Oslo]], [[Bonn]], [[Munich]], [[Stuttgart]], [[Turin]], [[Rome]] and [[Madrid]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.gandul.info/stiri/fiti-eroi-turul-doi-statul-isi-bate-joc-azi-romanii-strainatate-imagini-cozile-umilintei-update-campania-psd-acuza-presa-induce-sentimentul-e-organizat-corect-votul-sectii-goale-13566444 |title="FIȚI EROI ÎN TURUL DOI!". Statul își bate joc și azi de românii din străinătate. Imagini cu cozile umilinței. UPDATE: Campania PSD acuză presa că induce "sentimentul că nu e organizat corect votul": "Sunt secții goale!" |work=Gândul |author=Alina Matis |date=16 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> Once more, ACL and [[Monica Macovei]] urged the prolongation of voting process.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-esential-18573815-acl-cere-biroului-electora-central-prelungirea-programului-votare-strainatate.htm |title=ACL cere Biroului Electoral Central prelungirea programului de votare în străinătate |work=HotNews.ro |author=I.C. |date=16 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> Spontaneous protests broke out again in front of embassies and consulates in major European cities. Protesters expressed anger over Ponta's government and poor organization of the election.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ziare.com/alegeri/alegeri-prezidentiale-2014/diaspora-voteaza-cozi-uriase-proteste-si-imnul-national-live-1333580 |title=Diaspora votează: Circa 10.000 de români, la coadă în Londra |work=Ziare.com |author=Diana Toea |date=16 November 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> Shortly after the polls closed, angry voters forced the entrances into the embassies and consulates, to be able to exercise their right to vote. In [[Paris]] and [[Turin]], things degenerated into street fighting between voters and law enforcement.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/2014-11-16/romanian-presidential-race-too-close-to-call-exit-polls-show.html |title=Johannis Wins Romania Presidency in Double-Digit Comeback |work=Bloomberg |author=Andra Timu, Edith Balazs |date=16 November 2014}}</ref> Displeased voters were dispersed by police with [[tear gas]] and batons.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.reddit.com/r/europe/comments/2mhv4a/italian_and_french_police_evict_romanian_voters/ |title=Italian and French police evict Romanian voters from Romanian embassies using tear gas |work=Reddit |date=16 November 2014}}</ref> Four people were injured and one arrested after the intervention of [[Carabinieri]] in [[Turin]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.b1.ro/stiri/externe/patru-rani-i-i-un-roman-arestat-la-torino-dupa-interven-ia-poli-i-tilor-la-o-sec-ie-de-votare-foto-96113.html |title=Efectul organizării alegerilor în diaspora: Patru răniți și un român arestat la Torino, după intervenția polițiștilor la o secție de votare |work=B1.ro |date=17 November 2014 |language=ro |access-date=17 November 2014 |archive-date=29 November 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141129122605/http://www.b1.ro/stiri/externe/patru-rani-i-i-un-roman-arestat-la-torino-dupa-interven-ia-poli-i-tilor-la-o-sec-ie-de-votare-foto-96113.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> Having followed the election process, the chairman of the Commission for European Affairs in Bundestag, Gunther Krichbaum, suggested that the voting rights of Romanian citizens had been hindered to such an extent, that the Diaspora voting problems should be investigated as "fraud", and that [[Victor Ponta]] should withdraw from office, having lost all authority to serve the public, in any position or qualification.<ref name="ziare.com_2014-11-29">{{Citation | url=http://www.ziare.com/victor-ponta/premier/inalt-oficial-de-la-berlin-ponta-nu-mai-este-calificat-pentru-nicio-responsabilitate-in-stat-1334600| title=Inalt oficial de la Berlin: Ponta nu mai este calificat pentru nicio responsabilitate in stat| newspaper=Ziare.com| date= 21 November 2014| author=Ioana Ene Dogioiu| access-date=29 November 2014}}</ref><ref name="gunther-krichbaum.de/_2014-11-29">{{Citation | url=http://www.gunther-krichbaum.de/| title=Home| newspaper=Gunther-krichbaum.de/| author= Official Blog, para. 4| access-date=29 November 2014}}</ref>

=== Undercover officer allegations ===
In a worsening institutional conflict between the Presidency and the Government, outgoing President [[Traian Băsescu]] accused Prime Minister [[Victor Ponta]] of serving as an undercover intelligence officer between 1997 and 2001.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-romania-politics-idUSKCN0I30UG20141014 |title=Romania president says PM was an undercover spy |work=Reuters |author=Luiza Ilie |date=14 October 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/01/world/europe/presidential-candidates-spy-allegations-in-romania-conjure-a-dystopian-past.html |title=Spy Allegations in a Presidential Race Conjure Romania's Authoritarian Past |work=The New York Times |author=Andrew Higgins |date=31 October 2014}}</ref> Ponta dismissed the charge as "all lies".<ref>{{cite web |url=https://abcnews.go.com/International/wireStory/romanian-president-accuses-pm-spy-26179249 |title=Romanian President Accuses PM of Being an Ex-Spy |work=ABC News |author=Alison Mutler |date=14 October 2014}}</ref> His rival [[Klaus Iohannis]] demanded an immediate clarification of the situation,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-politic-18302119-klaus-iohanis-despre-scandalul-ponta-ofiter-acoperit-sie-solicit-lui-victor-ponta-clarifice-fata-natiunii-situatia-domniei-sale.htm |title=Klaus Iohanis, despre scandalul Ponta - ofițer acoperit SIE: Îi solicit lui Victor Ponta să clarifice în fața națiunii situația domniei sale |work=HotNews.ro |author=V.M. |date=14 October 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> while the Minister of Justice Robert Cazanciuc labelled Băsescu's statements as "campaign statements", and the topic as "ridiculous".<ref>{{cite web |url=http://business-review.eu/featured/romanian-president-says-prime-minister-acted-as-secret-intelligence-officer-71673 |title=Romanian president says prime-minister acted as secret intelligence officer |work=Business Review |date=14 October 2014}}</ref>

Espionage was already a talking point during the electoral campaign. [[Teodor Meleșcanu]], who ran the [[Foreign Intelligence Service (Romania)|Foreign Intelligence Service]], resigned in September and joined the presidential race as an independent candidate one day later. Around the same time, [[Robert Turcescu]], a popular television anchor, confessed live on air that he had been an undercover lieutenant-colonel for an espionage service and resigned his post.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.digi24.ro/Stiri/Digi24/Actualitate/Stiri/JURNALIST+ROBERT+TURCESCU+OFITER+SUB+ACOPERIRE |title=Jurnalistul Robert Turcescu a mărturisit că a fost ofițer acoperit. C. T. Popescu: Sunt uluit de acest delir mistic |work=Digi24 |date=21 September 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> Under Romanian law, outing oneself as a spy is illegal, but prosecutors did not press charges.

=== Alleged electoral bribe ===
Members of PMP and PNL expressed outrage over the announced distribution of 18&nbsp;kg of food to more than 6.5 million people during the electoral campaign, in October and November.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.nasul.tv/2014/10/05/exploziv-licitatie-ilegala-cu-fonduri-europene-pentru-mita-electorala-mascata-in-66-milioane-pachete-cu-18-kg-de-alimente/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141006051738/http://www.nasul.tv/2014/10/05/exploziv-licitatie-ilegala-cu-fonduri-europene-pentru-mita-electorala-mascata-in-66-milioane-pachete-cu-18-kg-de-alimente/ |url-status=dead |archive-date=6 October 2014 |title=Licitație ilegală cu fonduri europene pentru mită electorală mascată în 6,6 milioane pachete cu 18 kg de alimente |work=Nașul TV |author=Dorina Lascăr |date=5 October 2014 |language=ro }}</ref> In a press release, PNL stated that "in the mad rush for votes for presidential candidate Victor Ponta, PSD doesn't have the slightest reluctance to use EU funds for masked electoral bribe". This initiative was endorsed by the Ministry of European Funds, who published on 20 September a notice of auction in which the Romanian government said it wants to provide 6,652,986 food packages within the Fund of European aid for the most deprived persons.{{citation needed|date=November 2020}} More specifically, over 150,000 food packages would be sent to each county, totaling 100 million euros.{{citation needed|date=November 2020}} PNL argues that the way this auction is organized raises serious questions about its legality. The Minister for European Funds, [[Eugen Teodorovici]], said that EU funds are not used for electoral purposes and any claims of their diversion is "misinformation".{{citation needed|date=November 2020}}

President [[Traian Băsescu]] repeatedly stated that Victor Ponta "bribes the electorate" and "makes electoral alms from borrowed money".<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.romanialibera.ro/politica/institutii/18-30-declaratii-de-presa-traian-basescu-353242 |title=Traian Băsescu: Ponta și Iohannis sunt mincinoși și corupți. Nu îl susțin nici pe Ponta și nici pe Iohannis. Susțin candidatul PMP. Toată populația României îi plătește campania lui Ponta. Nu mai vorbim despre moralitatea lui Iohannis care are un proces deschis cu ANI. Nu îi consider pe niciunul demn de a fi președinte |work=România Liberă |author=Paul Filimon |date=13 October 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> In a press conference critical to Victor Ponta and Klaus Iohannis, Băsescu mentioned the figure of 4.8 billion euros, money that would go towards electoral alms and will be paid by the population.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/politic/basescu-nu-i-sustin-si-nu-ii-voi-sustine-nici-pe-ponta-nici-pe-iohannis-la-prezidentiale-raman-consecvent-in-a-o-sustine-pe-elena-udrea-declaratiile-presedintelui-13380027 |title=Băsescu: Nu-i susțin și nu îi voi susține nici pe Ponta, nici pe Iohannis la prezidențiale. Rămân consecvent în a o susține pe Elena Udrea. DECLARAȚIILE președintelui |work=Mediafax.ro |author=Irina Tacu, Valentina Postelnicu |date=13 October 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

During a large meeting in [[Iași]], [[Klaus Iohannis]] mentioned that Ponta's figure is on each pole and tree, asking rhetorically where the money for his campaign came from. He also stated that every Romanian pays Ponta's campaign from the taxes and dues he introduced.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.realitatea.net/iohannis--de-unde-provin-banii-de-campanie-ai-lui-ponta-sunt-bani-din-taxe-si-impozite--bani-din-coruptie_1549886.html |title=Iohannis: De unde provin banii de campanie ai lui Ponta? Sunt bani din taxe și impozite, bani din corupție? |work=Realitatea.net |date=18 October 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> During the same meeting, Iohannis refuted all rumors regarding his intentions to cut the pensions after the election, after many pensioners received flyers in the mail, with messages such as "Only Ponta protects the pensions" and "Klaus Iohannis wants to cut your pension" written on them.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ziuaconstanta.ro/stiri/politic/fluturasii-electorali-zboara-liberi-prin-judet-pensionarii-denunta-campania-denigratoare-pe-care-psd-516501.html |title=Pensionarii denunță "campania denigratoare" pe care PSD o face prin poștă |work=Ziua de Constanța |author=Nicoleta Nicolau |date=18 October 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> In a press release, ACL accused PSD that it engages in a campaign against Klaus Iohannis by misinforming and deceiving voters.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ziare.com/alegeri/alegeri-prezidentiale-2014/psd-si-posta-romana-acuzati-ca-trimit-pensionarilor-pliante-anti-iohannis-1327822 |title=PSD și Poșta Română, acuzați că trimit pensionarilor pliante anti-Iohannis |work=Ziare.com |date=15 October 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> The [[Romanian Post]] signed contracts with PSD, but also with PMP, Macovei and Tăriceanu, agreeing to send newspapers, catalogs, leaflets, brochures and other electoral advertising materials to homes around the country.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/politic/posta-romana-sunt-contracte-si-cu-macovei-udrea-si-tariceanu-pe-distribuirea-de-material-electoral-13424402 |title=Poșta Română: Sunt contracte și cu Macovei, Udrea și Tăriceanu pe distribuirea de material electoral |work=Mediafax |date=20 October 2014 |language=ro}}</ref> Over 4 million anti-Iohannis flyers were distributed by the Romanian Post, totaling up to 50,000 euros.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.gandul.info/politica/cat-l-au-costat-pe-ponta-cei-4-milioane-de-fluturasi-anti-iohannis-impartiti-de-posta-romana-cu-talonul-de-pensie-13701926 |title=Cât l-au costat pe Ponta cei 4 milioane de fluturaşi anti-Iohannis, împărţiţi de Poşta Română cu talonul de pensie |work=Gândul |author=Cristian Andrei |date=4 December 2014 |language=ro}}</ref>

=== Vote rigging in Moldova ===
Sebastian Ghiță, PSD deputy and Victor Ponta's fellow, would be part of a pyramidal mechanism of defrauding the 2014 presidential election, according to prosecutors from the [[National Anticorruption Directorate]], [[Ploiești]] branch. He would have given money from illegal deals to persuade voters from [[Moldova]] to elect Ponta as president.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ziare.com/sebastian-ghita/dna/dna-sebastian-ghita-a-cumparat-cu-bani-negri-alegatori-pentru-ponta-in-r-moldova-1369932 |title=DNA: Sebastian Ghita a cumparat cu bani negri alegatori pentru Ponta in R.Moldova |work=Ziare.com |date=24 June 2015 |language=ro}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/25/world/europe/romania-from-frying-pan-to-legal-fire.html |title=Romania: From Frying Pan to Legal Fire |work=The New York Times |date=24 June 2015}}</ref>

Sebastian Ghiță would hand in the PSD headquarters in [[Bucharest]] 400,000 euros to Alin Petran, an intermediary sent over the Prut to gather the necessary votes.<ref name="frauda">{{cite web |url=http://www.digi24.ro/Stiri/Digi24/Actualitate/Justitie/Noi+acuzatii+pentru+Sebastian+Ghita+El+este+asteptat+la+DNA+Ploi |title=EXCLUSIV. S. Ghiță, mecanism piramidal pentru fraudă la prezidențiale. Martor: Victor Ponta era la curent |work=Digi24 |date=24 June 2015 |language=ro}}</ref> Subsequently, the intermediary has recruited ten coordinators who, in turn, managed 200 people. Each was responsible to provide between 50 and 100 votes to the social democrat candidate. Electors who demonstrated that voted with Victor Ponta received watches, clothes or food.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.gandul.info/stiri/finantarea-campaniei-victor-ponta-republica-moldova-investigata-procurori-sponsorul-sebastian-ghita-iesirea-dna-depune-plangere-procurorul-general-impotriva-oamenilor-vor-lovitura-palat-romania-14494961 |title=Finanţarea campaniei lui Victor Ponta în Republica Moldova, INVESTIGATĂ de procurori. Sponsorul Sebastian Ghiţă, la ieşirea de la DNA: "Voi depune plângere la Procurorul General împotriva oamenilor care vor o lovitură de palat în România" |work=Gândul |last1=Popescu |first=Andrei Luca |last2=Ilie |first2=Daciana |date=24 June 2015 |language=ro}}</ref> Total costs of these operations were estimated at 350,000 euros.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/europe/romanian-pms-aide-indicted-for-corruption-charges/2015/06/24/99aac7aa-1a66-11e5-bed8-1093ee58dad0_story.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150626225439/http://www.washingtonpost.com/world/europe/romanian-pms-aide-indicted-for-corruption-charges/2015/06/24/99aac7aa-1a66-11e5-bed8-1093ee58dad0_story.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=26 June 2015 |title=Romanian premier's aide indicted for corruption charges |newspaper=The Washington Post |date=24 June 2015}}</ref><ref name="ghita">{{cite web |url=http://www.mediafax.ro/politic/sebastian-ghita-urmarit-trafic-influenta-spalare-bani-coruperea-alegatorilor-mi-interzice-parasesc-ploiestiul-probabil-umilit-interdictie-vorbi-victor-ponta-14494045 |title=Sebastian Ghiţă, urmărit pentru trafic de influenţă, spălare de bani şi coruperea alegătorilor: "Mi se interzice să părăsesc Ploieştiul, probabil pentru a fi umilit. Am interdicţie de a vorbi cu Victor Ponta" |work=Mediafax |last=Hera |first=Mona |date=24 June 2015 |language=ro}}</ref> Investigators also determined that Sebastian Ghiță and his friends would have created a database that included 20,000 Romanian citizens from Moldova, with voting rights in the 2014 presidential election. According to a witness, Victor Ponta was aware "about this fraudulent attempt to win the presidential election".<ref name="frauda" />

As of 24 June 2015, Sebastian Ghiță is prosecuted for [[influence peddling]], [[money laundering]] and bribing the voters.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://stirileprotv.ro/stiri/actualitate/surse-procurorii-dna-extind-urmarirea-penala-impotriva-lui-sebastian-ghita-deputatul-este-acuzat-de-noi-fapte-de-coruptie.html |title=Cele trei masuri luate de DNA impotriva lui Sebastian Ghita. Cum ar fi corupt alegatorii cu tigai de pe piata neagra |work=Stirile Pro TV |date=24 June 2015 |language=ro}}</ref> Moreover, Ghiță is forbidden to exercise his function of deputy, a premiere in the Romanian justice, but also to talk with Victor Ponta or to leave Ploiești.<ref name="ghita" /> Ghiță accuses a "prosecutors [[coup]]", in an attempt to overthrow the Ponta Government.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://stirileprotv.ro/stiri/politic/sebastian-ghita-cere-ajutorul-colegilor-din-camera-deputatilor-dupa-ce-dna-l-a-suspendat-din-parlament-este-un-abuz.html |title=Ghita anunta o "lovitura de palat a procurorilor". Imperiul PSD contraataca: ce replica pentru DNA au social-democratii |work=Stirile Pro TV |date=25 June 2015 |language=ro}}</ref>

=== Cyber attacks ===
In a debate organized by the PNL parliamentary group on 12 February 2015, Marcel Opriș, head of the Special Telecommunications Service (STS), stated that during the presidential election were used [[cyber attack]]s for political purposes,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.gandul.info/stiri/directorul-sts-la-prezidentiale-au-fost-atacuri-cibernetice-in-scop-politic-fiind-implicat-un-post-tv-13817363 |title=Directorul STS: La prezidențiale au fost atacuri cibernetice în scop politic, fiind implicat un post TV |work=Gândul |author=Andi Manciu |date=12 February 2015 |language=ro}}</ref> being involved a Romanian television through which a signal was given for "a devastating qualified attack for IT-ists".<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-esential-19360717-marcel-opris-sts-atacurile-cibernetice-pot-folosite-scopuri-politice-episod-petrecut-perioada-prezidentialelor.htm |title=Marcel Opriș (STS): Atacurile cibernetice pot fi folosite în scopuri politice; un episod s-a petrecut în perioada prezidențialelor |work=HotNews.ro |author=R. M. |date=12 February 2015 |language=ro}}</ref> PNL deputy Mihăiță Calimente announced he'll propose at the Defence Commission of the [[Chamber of Deputies of Romania|Chamber of Deputies]] as the director of STS to be heard on this subject.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.cotidianul.ro/opris-un-atac-cibernetic-s-a-petrecut-in-perioada-prezidentialelor-256584/ |title=Opriș: Un atac cibernetic s-a petrecut în perioada prezidențialelor |work=Cotidianul.ro |author=Paul Dumitrescu |date=12 February 2015 |language=ro}}</ref>

